# Licensed pixel-art pack and audio: usable locally, not redistributed whole.
#
# The owner's licence covers using these in this product, which is not the same
# as republishing the artwork. The redistributable part -- the UI frames the
# engine chrome actually draws with (dialogue plate, heart HUD, two emotes, the
# arrow, the pixel face) and the audio -- now lives inside the package at
# ahafrog/assets/, so it ships with a pip install and is tracked there.
#
# This directory is the owner's local copy of the FULL pack: character art,
# monsters, terrain and the other ~1850 files, which are never published.
# The /assets mount reads this directory first and falls back to the package
# per file, so dropping the full pack here -- with its own catalog.json --
# re-activates it locally without changing anything that gets published.
#
# Leading slash matters: a bare "assets/" is unanchored and would also match
# ahafrog/assets/, un-shipping the files above.
/assets/

